emonstrate professionalism with students, faculty, staff, and administration Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills.  Timely attendance at all required class periods and other program activities (if required). Complete all required training, including training on LMS and testing software. Collaborate with other faculty to enhance course materials and contribute to program development initiatives. REQUIREMENTS:   Earned terminal clinical doctoral degree in physical therapy (DPT or t-DPT). Licensed (or eligible for licensure) to practice physical therapy in Kansas. At least one year of full-time licensed work as a physical therapists in the United States. Ability to teach on campus in Leavenworth, Kansas.   PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:   Experience teaching in a college/university program. Specialization certification from American Board of Physical Therapy Specialties (ABPTS) TO APPLY:  Submit a cover letter, resume and contact information for at least three current professional references.  Saint Mary is an Equal Opportunity Employer.  Questions: email human resources at  hr@stmary.edu",
